       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered the order. I can't put in a dose 5 times the maximum without a documented clinical reason, because the patient could be seriously harmed.\n\nThere's no recognized clinical situation where amlodipine 50 mg/day is appropriate. The labeled maximum is 10 mg/day. Your patient is a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, which gives no reason to go beyond standard dosing. At 50 mg/day, profound hypotension, shock and noncardiogenic pulmonary edema are real risks. Amlodipine stays in the body a long time, so that toxicity can last for days.\n\n\"I confirm\" may have been meant for 5 mg, the option I listed first. It's an easy mix-up, so I'd rather check than guess.\n\nHere's how we can proceed:\n\n1. **If you meant 5 mg (or 10 mg):** tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **If you really intend 50 mg:** tell me the clinical reason, and please have a clinical pharmacist or the attending review it. I'll then enter the order with the reason and the reviewer's name in the order note.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
